      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Lord, please. Any stat that can be viewed in avatar parameters should be able to be limited with as much or as little granularity as the host wants at the time of instance creation.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-03-11T23:10:40.548Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I am expanding on this feature request, since I think a slightly different and more clarified feature is in order. \n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/allow-world-creators-to-set-avatar-limits-for-public-instances\n\n**Allow instance creators to define avatar restrictions for their instance**\n\nThis would include:\n\n- Instance owners setting world-specific avatar restrictions\n\n- The users having the option to enable or disable the restriction for themselves (probably default \"on\" each join)\n\nThis would help event worlds moderate their instances to prevent users from running horrendously optimized avatars. \n\nPart of this feature request would be more impactful if we had granular avatar blocking, for example:\n\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/granular-safety-settings\n\nI was also going to suggest an optional \"strict enforcement\" for instances, but I think the user being able to choose it for themselves would be sufficient.",
